Notes on the ISA.

1. The most interesting part of the ISA is the Code Morphing Software (CMS). CMS takes in X86 compatible instructions and converts them into VLIW instructions compatible with ntive hardware.
2. The advantages of this approach is that the VLIW engine can be modified anytime with just minor changes to the ISA.
3. The processor will be compatible with the newer versions of the X86 instructions as long as the code morphing software is updated.
4. The code morphing software supports different execution modes for the X86 compatible instructions such as interpretation, interpretation with code generation, and optimization.
5. CMS uses instrumentation to predict which mode of execution to pick.
6. Importantly, the X86 instructions are processed in order. However, the work of the instructions is done out-of-order.
